dsh-devin-search-next is independent of DeepSeek Harness, Devin/Windsurf and piwin.

Protocol field numbers, role encoding, OAuth endpoint/PKCE conventions and
completion message design were adapted from these MIT-licensed piwin sources:
  packages/agent-host/src/devin/oauth.ts
  packages/tools-web/src/devin-search-provider.ts
  packages/host-runtime/src/code-search/backends/windsurf-protobuf.ts
  packages/host-runtime/src/code-search/backends/windsurf-protocol.ts
  packages/host-runtime/src/code-search/completion-port.ts
Copyright (c) 2026 Piwin contributors. See LICENSE for the MIT permission notice.

The pure-logic modules under `lib/core/` are mechanically ported (type-erased,
behavior-identical) from the MIT-licensed `dsh-devin-search` implementation, and
the npm `ignore` dependency was replaced by the bundled `lib/core/gitignore.js`.
This package imports no piwin package and reads no piwin credential file.

The implementation is a smaller independent client with strict framing, bounded
IO and an allowlisted local search loop. DSH service integration was verified
against DeepSeek Harness 0.2.1-rc.3 (bundle gate, tool registration, web search
provider selection, browser routes, client slots).

Offline fixtures do not establish compatibility with a live provider, account
entitlements, service availability, prices, or continued authorization.
